   "summary": "Transparent Tribe (APT-C-56) has been observed deploying a new custom backdoor called PATCHCORD against Afghan telecom providers and South Asian critical infrastructure, alongside a Go-based implant named SHEETCORD that uses Google Sheets for command-and-control. The group also conducted multistage attacks using LNK shortcuts hidden in disguised image or archive files to execute malicious scripts and establish persistent access. Reported malware families include PATCHCORD, SHEETCORD, HACKERAI C2 Agent, SHEETCREEP, ValleyRAT, and GateSentinel, with targeting across telecommunications, government, defense, energy, and healthcare sectors."
